The analyst is responsible for maintaining the chain of custody procedures during this step. 
In order to determine the appropriate analyses to be performed, the analyst may need access 
to the information given in the sampling data sheet. The analyst may register all subsamples 
taken for analysis in the sample record form . Additionally, for every sample a sample 
preparation sheet shall be filled in including, at least, the following information: 
 Sample code; 
 Subsample volume; 
 Preparation procedure and date; 
 Aliquot code; 
 Analyst name. 
The analyses performed to the aliquots with the different instrumental techniques generate 
data files which must be coded and registered so that they are unequivocally linked to the 
corresponding aliquot. An analytical data sheet shall contain: 
 Sample code; 
 Aliquot code; 
 Instrumental technique; 
 Analytical method; 
 Date of analysis; 
 Analyst name
